<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>
</ix:nonNumeric>

<div>&#160;</div>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><b>Analysis of the Information Presented in the Pay Versus Performance Table</b>&#160;<b> </b></p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">We generally seek to incentivize long-term performance and therefore do not specifically align our performance measures with &#8220;compensation actually paid,&#8221; as calculated in accordance with Item 402(v) of Regulation S-K, for a particular fiscal year. In accordance with Item 402(v), the following describes the relationships between compensation actually paid and the financial performance measures presented in the Pay Versus Performance Table.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><b>Compensation Actually Paid and Total Shareholder Return</b></p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">From fiscal 2025 to fiscal 2026, compensation actually paid to the PEO decreased from $2,272,752 to $(6,331,600), while the value of an initial fixed $100 investment based on cumulative TSR decreased from $280 to approximately $129. The decrease in compensation actually paid to the PEO was principally attributable to the decrease in the fair value of outstanding unvested equity awards resulting from the decline in the market price of the Company&#8217;s Common Stock during fiscal 2026.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">From fiscal 2024 to fiscal 2025, compensation actually paid to the PEO decreased from $5,798,880 to $2,272,752, while the value of an initial fixed $100 investment based on cumulative TSR increased from $277 to $280. Average compensation actually paid to the non-PEO NEOs decreased from $348,825 in fiscal 2025 to $225,200 in fiscal 2026, while cumulative TSR decreased from $280 to approximately $129. The decrease in average compensation actually paid to the Non-PEO NEOs was principally attributable to changes in the fair value of outstanding and vesting equity awards.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">From fiscal 2024 to fiscal 2025, average compensation actually paid to the non-PEO NEOs decreased from $448,750 to $348,825, while cumulative TSR increased from $277 to $280.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><b>Compensation Actually Paid and Net Income </b></p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">Net income increased from $6,617,821 in fiscal 2025 to $7,401,683 in fiscal 2026, an increase of $783,862, or approximately 12%, while compensation actually paid to the PEO decreased from $2,272,752 to $(6,331,600) and average compensation actually paid to the non-PEO NEOs decreased from $348,825 to $225,200.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">Net income increased from $5,408,645 in fiscal 2024 to $6,617,821 in fiscal 2025, an increase of $1,209,176, or approximately 22%, while compensation actually paid to the PEO decreased from $5,798,880 to $2,272,752 and average compensation actually paid to the non-PEO NEOs decreased from $448,750 to $348,825.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">The Company has not historically used net income as a specific performance measure for purposes of determining executive compensation. Accordingly, changes in compensation actually paid may not correspond directly with changes in the Company&#8217;s reported net income.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><b>Compensation Actually Paid and Cumulative TSR</b></p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;">The Company has not historically used TSR as a specific performance measure in determining annual executive compensation. However, because the calculation of compensation actually paid under Item 402(v) includes changes in the fair value of outstanding equity awards, changes in the market price of the Company&#8217;s Common Stock can significantly affect compensation actually paid even when the underlying compensation arrangements have not changed.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;"><i>All information provided above under the </i>&#8220;<i>Pay Versus Performance</i>&#8221;<i> heading will not be deemed to be incorporated by reference in any filing of the Company under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, or the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, whether made before or after the date hereof and irrespective of any general incorporation language in any such filing.</i>&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<div class="PGBK" style="width: 100%; margin-left: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt">
<div class="PGFTR" style="text-align: center; width: 100%">
<div class="hf-row">
<div class="hf-cell PGNUM">&#160;</div>
</div>
</div>

